  <page_number>96</page_number>
  <running_head>P. VOET</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Go-</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">armis superior, prostrato Fron-</l>
    <l n="2">tino privatæ victoriæ, publi-</l>
    <l n="3">cam adjungeret, passimque di-</l>
    <l n="4">vulsa Danorum[?] agmina pro-</l>
    <l n="5">fligaret.</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">Sic itidem Ericus exercitus</l>
    <l n="7">Norwegiani dux exercitatissi-</l>
    <l n="8">mus cum Alarico Suenonum</l>
    <l n="9">Rege duellum suscipit. Et qui</l>
    <l n="10">certa clade affectus fuisset, si</l>
    <l n="11">exercitus certamine pugna</l>
    <l n="12">confecta fuisset, ille victoriam</l>
    <l n="13">retulit,dum forte privato con-</l>
    <l n="14">gressui dabatur locus. Prode-</l>
    <l n="15">unt enim in circum Alaricus</l>
    <l n="16">&amp; Ericus,acerrimè &amp; infensis-</l>
    <l n="17">simè utrinque depugnantes.</l>
    <l n="18">Et quamvis corporum robore</l>
    <l n="19">ac militari disciplinâ visi sint</l>
    <l n="20">æquè pares, adeo ut uterque</l>
    <l n="21">gravissimis plagis affectus in</l>
    <l n="22">circo corruerit moribundus:</l>
    <l n="23">certaminis tamen singularis</l>
    <l n="24">fortuna, quæ Alaricum è vivis</l>
    <l n="25">confestim abstulit, Ericum æ-</l>
    <l n="26">grè curatum vitæ restituit,</l>
  </main_text>
  <marginalia>
    <note side="left" at="armis superior, prostrato" line_from="1" line_to="1">Johan. Magn. 1. 4. Histor. Gothic.</note>
  </marginalia>
  <notes>The word after "Danorum" is printed with a mark under the a that looks like an ogonek, so the reading "Danorum" is doubtful. The catchword "Go-" is at the lower right. The faint text at the bottom right corner is the digitiser's mark and is omitted.</notes>
</page>
